; Original Brickwright CARDIAC example: one decision per input sample.
; Numeric I/O is historical; a circuit adapter is a modern Brickwright device.
; OUT emits memory, so each branch stores its decision before output.
ORG 01
ENTRY again
again: INP sample
       CLA sample
       SUB threshold
       TAC dark
       CLA zero
       STO decision
       OUT decision
       JMP again
dark:  CLA one
       STO decision
       OUT decision
       JMP again
ORG 80
sample:    DAT 0
threshold: DAT 500
one:       DAT 1
zero:      DAT 0
decision:  DAT 0
